VALUES
  (
    2,
    'How to Use Storytelling to Build Your Startup’s Culture',
    'how-to-use-storytelling-to-build-your-startup-s-culture',
    'In a fast-moving startup, your culture becomes the backbone of how your team thinks, works, and grows. One of the most powerful ways to build that culture is through storytelling. Stories connect people emotionally, give meaning to everyday tasks, and help everyone understand why the company exists beyond just profits.',
    '<p>How to Use Storytelling to Build Your Startup’s Culture</p><p></p><p>In a fast-moving startup, your culture becomes the backbone of how your team thinks, works, and grows. One of the most powerful ways to build that culture is through storytelling. Stories connect people emotionally, give meaning to everyday tasks, and help everyone understand why the company exists beyond just profits.</p><p></p><p>Start by sharing the origin story of your startup—why you started, what problem inspired you, and what moment made you take action. This helps your team connect to the mission on a deeper level. Next, highlight real customer stories. When your team sees how your product changes lives or solves real frustrations, they feel more motivated and aligned with your purpose.</p><p></p><p>Use internal stories too. Celebrate team wins, talk about challenges openly, and share lessons from failures. These stories reinforce values like resilience, teamwork, innovation, and transparency. Encourage your team members to share their own stories during meetings or internal chats. When storytelling becomes part of everyday communication, your culture becomes stronger, more human, and more united.</p><p></p><p>In the end, storytelling is not about creating fictional narratives—it’s about capturing real experiences that remind everyone what your startup stands for. When done consistently, it turns your mission and values into something people can feel, not just read on a slide.</p>',
    'Genesis Team',
    1,
    'https://media.genesis-quic.in/blogs/1764100349620-dtduwxf-4931732341324.jpg',
    0,
    'published',
    24,
    0,
    '2025-11-25 19:52:33',
    '2025-11-25 19:52:35',
    '2026-08-11 08:27:26'
  );
