VALUES
  (
    3,
    'Most Entrepreneurs Start Later in Life Than You Think',
    'most-entrepreneurs-start-later-in-life-than-you-think',
    'There’s a common belief that entrepreneurship is a young person’s game - but the reality is very different. Most successful entrepreneurs actually start later in life, often in their 30s, 40s, or even 50s.',
    '<p>There’s a common belief that entrepreneurship is a young person’s game—but the reality is very different. Most successful entrepreneurs actually start later in life, often in their 30s, 40s, or even 50s. Experience, industry knowledge, and financial stability play a huge role in building a long-lasting business, and these are strengths that usually grow with age.</p><p></p><p>Studies show that older founders tend to build more sustainable companies because they understand customers better, have stronger professional networks, and make decisions based on real-world insights rather than guesswork. They’ve worked in different roles, faced challenges, and learned from failures—giving them a more grounded approach to entrepreneurship.</p><p></p><p>The myth of the “young genius founder” can create unnecessary pressure, but the truth is that there is no perfect age to start. Entrepreneurship is about solving problems, not about how old you are. Whether you’re 20 or 50, if you have a clear vision and the determination to execute it, the right time to start is whenever you’re ready.</p><p></p><p>So, if you feel like you\'re “late,” remember—many of the world’s most impactful entrepreneurs started exactly where you are now. What matters is the courage to take the first step.</p>',
    'Genesis Team',
    1,
    'https://media.genesis-quic.in/blogs/1764100453429-b9c5bef-3201732336658.jpg',
    0,
    'published',
    29,
    0,
    '2025-11-25 19:54:42',
    '2025-11-25 19:54:44',
    '2026-08-11 08:27:27'
  );
